        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "83201b80-6f29-58cd-bc22-745fbc820aeb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mark Fulton, Billy Wright\n- Organizations: Loyalist Volunteer Force, Irish National Liberation Army\n- Places: Maze Prison, Northern Ireland\n- Events: The Troubles, assassination of Billy Wright\n- Roles: LVF leader, Ulster loyalist\n\nFacts:\n- Billy Wright was born on 7 July 1960 and died on 27 December 1997.\n- Billy Wright was a prominent Ulster loyalist during the ethno-nationalist conflict in Northern Ireland known as the Troubles.\n- In 1997, members of the Irish National Liberation Army assassinated Billy Wright in the Maze Prison.\n- After Billy Wright's 1997 assassination, Mark Fulton took over command of the Loyalist Volunteer Force.\n- Mark Fulton became the leader of the Loyalist Volunteer Force after succeeding Billy Wright.",
